ARCHITECTURE (ADR-002/004/005/006/013/014/015)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - DrivingDynamicsPage (SwiftUI View) + @Observable DrivingDynamicsPageModel.
    No business logic in the view body; all data via the model.
  - Data seam DrivingDynamicsDataSource keeps the web hook names verbatim at the
    Swift call sites: useMotorLatest, useMotorHistory, useDrives, useDrivingCoach,
    useDriveDynamicsLatest (G-force/pedal), useAutopilot (vehicle-state speed +
    cruise). Only this file changes when the generated client lands (P1/S2-S3).
  - Panels reproduced (every web <GlassPanel>/region, same data + order):
      LiveMotorStatus · GForcePanel · PedalUsage · SpeedGearPanel · AutopilotSection
      · MotorHistoryCharts (power/torque/rpm) · MotorEfficiencyInsights (3 panels)
      · SummaryStats (6 cards) · DrivingCoachSection (score gauge, style breakdown,
      efficiency, weekly trend, pattern bars, recommendations, per-drive table)
      · DriveAnalyticsSection (speed distribution, acceleration scatter, power
      profile, date range) · DrivingTips.
  - Charts use the P3 native Swift Charts wrappers (TSChartContainer + TSLineChart /
    TSAreaChart / TSScatterChart); the categorical speed distribution renders as
    native labeled bars. No WKWebView, no direct `import Charts` in the feature.
  - Units: every physical quantity is stored/derived in SI (Nm, rpm, °C, m, m/s, W,
    Wh) and converted ONLY at the render boundary via the shared Units facade
    (Units.convertSpeed/Distance/Temperature) keyed off @Environment(\.tsUnits)
    (P1/S5). Coach Wh/km + km are endpoint-display-shaped (no SI conversion), as web.
  - i18n: DrivingDynamicsStrings folds the web keys onto the catalog's
    `translation.dynamics.*` entries (ADR-014); 109 keys pre-existed, +15 added.
  - a11y: accessibilityLabel/value on gauges + cards, header traits on section
    titles, >=44pt controls, light/dark/high-contrast tokens, Dynamic Type (ADR-015).
  - Live freshness: model.isStale surfaces a ">2 min" chip (ADR-013).
  - Navigation: typed DrivingDynamicsLink NavigationDestination +
    DrivingDynamicsRouteRegistration.make() factory, mirroring the sibling unrouted
    RouteEfficiencyRouteRegistration; deep link /driving-dynamics -> .driving added
    to AppRouteParser (like /route-efficiency, /drive-score). The .driving enum host
    stays owned by DriveScorePage (no predecessor bypass, ADR honesty #7).

